gus (pseudonym) is an Estonian stencil artist based in Tartu. His works have earned the attention of the media and many art critics, been presented in art exhibitions and sold in art auctions.", "newValue": "Edward von Lõngus, the enigmatic Estonian stencil artist operating under a pseudonym, emerged from the vibrant street art scene of Tartu in the early 21st century to become a pivotal figure in contemporary public art. His distinctive style, often combining sharp social commentary with intricate stencil work and augmented reality (AR) technology, garnered significant media attention and critical acclaim across Europe. Lõngus's work uniquely bridges the ephemeral nature of street art with the institutional recognition of gallery spaces, challenging traditional perceptions of art's accessibility and value.

His artistic repertoire frequently features characters drawn from Estonian folklore, such as the 'Cannibal's Bride' and the giants Kalevipoeg and Vanapagan, recontextualized within modern urban settings. Notable installations include the 'Smartass' series, which integrated AR to bring his static murals to life via smartphone apps, and his high-profile project 'Walden X' (2018), which saw his works exhibited in multiple European capitals, including Brussels, Rome, and Paris, as part of Estonia's European Council Presidency cultural program. This initiative, supported by the Estonian Ministry of Culture, marked a significant moment for street art's elevation into cultural diplomacy, reaching an estimated 500,000 viewers.

